plexus-archiver-symlink-extraction-bypass -- repro / gate log   (REAL-APP-HTTP rebuild, 2026-07-16)
====================================================================================================
CVE-2018-1002200 (ZipSlip "../" write outside dest; fixed 3.6.0)  ->  CVE-2023-37460 (dangling-symlink
extraction escape; INCOMPLETE fix of CVE-2018-1002200; fixed 4.8.0).  Sink: AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile.
CWE-22 / CWE-61.  Variant A (same sink, same state-write escape channel /work/out/flag).

RUN MODE = real-app-http, external_http_trigger=true, runs_real_software=true, is_verbatim_lift=false.
The extraction is triggered by an EXTERNAL HTTP ARCHIVE UPLOAD (POST /extract), NOT an in-process driver.

REAL Java HTTP upload service (com.pcb.ExtractHttpService, JDK built-in com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer):
  GET  /health   -> 200 OK (readiness)
  POST /extract  (raw request body = the uploaded .tar; Content-Type application/x-tar):
       write upload -> temp file; TarUnArchiver ua = new TarUnArchiver(); ua.setSourceFile(uploaded);
       ua.setDestDirectory(/work/dest); ua.extract();  -- the REAL, unmodified published extract() path
       through AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile. After extraction the service checks the escape witness
       /work/out/flag (OUTSIDE /work/dest) and returns {"witness":<content>,"witness_exists":..,"error":..}.
  State reset per request: fresh empty /work/dest, /work/out kept, /work/out/flag deleted (so the residual's
  symlink is genuinely dangling) -> each external upload is an independent probe.

Faithful-core recipe: Maven pulls the EXACT published org.codehaus.plexus:plexus-archiver at
3.5 / 3.6.0 / 4.8.0 (+ transitive deps) from Maven Central; the HTTP service drives the REAL, unmodified
org.codehaus.plexus.archiver.tar.TarUnArchiver.extract() (base class AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile).
No plexus code edited. Benign state-write canary: ${PCB_FLAG} is the UPLOADED archive's payload content;
success = it is written to /work/out/flag OUTSIDE the extraction dir /work/dest and echoed in the response.

Jar availability (Maven Central, HTTP 200): 3.5, 3.6.0, 4.7.1, 4.8.0.

CONTAINMENT EVOLUTION (verbatim, AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile):
  V0 = 3.5   : NO containment check. `final File f = FileUtils.resolveFile( dir, entryName );` then
               `out = new FileOutputStream( f );` -- any "../" entry escapes.
  V1 = 3.6.0 : CVE-2018-1002200 fix adds
                 String canonicalDirPath  = dir.getCanonicalPath();
                 String canonicalDestPath = f.getCanonicalPath();
                 if ( !canonicalDestPath.startsWith( canonicalDirPath ) )
                     throw new ArchiverException( "Entry is outside of the target directory (" + entryName + ")" );
               write still `new FileOutputStream( f )` (follows symlinks); NO isSymbolicLink guard.
  V2 = 4.8.0 : CVE-2023-37460 fix adds, after the canonical check:
                 // don't allow override target symlink by standard file
                 if ( StringUtils.isEmpty( symlinkDestination ) && Files.isSymbolicLink( canonicalDestPath ) )
                     throw new ArchiverException( "Entry is outside of the target directory (" + entryName + ")" );

WHY THE FIX IS INCOMPLETE (JFrog XRAY-526292 / GHSA-wh3p-fphp-9h2m): for a DANGLING symlink (target does
not exist) the JVM realpath() returns NULL for the target, so getCanonicalPath() returns the symlink's
OWN SOURCE path inside dest -> the 3.6.0 `.startsWith(dir)` check PASSES -> the following regular-file
write follows the link and lands OUTSIDE dest. 4.8.0's isSymbolicLink guard closes it.

ORIGINAL (CVE-2018-1002200) uploaded tar  = one plain regular-file entry named "../out/flag" (content=FLAG).
RESIDUAL (CVE-2023-37460) uploaded tar    = two SAME-NAME entries, in order:
    (1) SYMLINK  entry "entry1" -> "/work/out/flag"   (dangling; /work/out exists, /work/out/flag absent)
    (2) REGULAR  entry "entry1"  content=FLAG          (write follows the entry1 symlink to /work/out/flag)

